---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout
  title="APIs & Feeds"
  description="The public API and STIX feed have been retired; a supported paid offering is planned."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Research', href: '/research/' }, { label: 'APIs & Feeds' }]}
  maxWidth="wide"
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl space-y-4" aria-labelledby="api-retired">
    <h1 id="api-retired" class="text-3xl font-bold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)]">APIs &amp; Feeds: retired</h1>
    <p class="text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
      The public JSON endpoints (<code>/api/qif.json</code>, <code>/api/tara.json</code>,
      <code>/api/stix.json</code>, <code>/api/navigator.json</code>) were retired on 2026-10-17 and now return 404.
      A supported API and STIX feed is planned as a paid feature; no date is set.
    </p>
    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold font-[family-name:var(--font-heading)] pt-2">What stays available</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-[var(--color-text-muted)]">
      <li>
        The registrar data stays open in the
        <a class="text-[var(--color-accent-primary)] hover:underline" href="https://github.com/qinnovates/neurosecurity/blob/main/datalake/qtara-registrar.json" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">repository</a>
        under the repository licence. It is a file, not a service: no uptime or format guarantee.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>qtara</code> 0.4.0 on PyPI is deprecated and bundles a snapshot of the registrar. It will not be updated.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
